# Repro for OpenMLS §4.7 AppDataUpdate validation gap (CONFIRMED 2026-10-17)

Confirmed on upstream main be2368a21ec5e0380abd568821addc57b79013ea and fork mimid-0.9.1 (d052e729). Not reported upstream (needs Mark's OK).

Cause: validate_app_data_update_proposals_and_group_context (openmls/src/group/public_group/validation.rs:737 main / :653 fork): on the first Remove it does return Ok(()) when the commit has no GroupContextExtensions proposal (or it lacks app_data_dictionary) — the normal case — skipping duplicate-remove, remove+update, and remove-of-absent checks for every component. With a GCE present, 'absent' is judged against the proposal's dictionary, not the current GroupContext. Same function runs in the commit builder (commit_builder.rs:1075 main) and receiver (staged_commit.rs:199 main), so stock OpenMLS builds these invalid commits. apply_proposals.rs:283 discards the remove result. MoreThanOneRemovePerComponentId (errors.rs:865) is never returned. ProposalQueue::add dedups identical ProposalRefs (code reading only).

Results (receiver accepts and merges; epoch authenticators match): a) remove(X) by-ref + remove(X) inline; b) remove(X)+update(X); c) remove(Z) with no data; d1) valid remove(X) then remove(Y)+update(Y); d2) valid remove(X) then remove(Z). Controls with a GCE carrying the unchanged dictionary are refused (CombinedRemoveAndUpdateOperations / CannotRemoveNonexistentComponent).

Patched scratch copy: all 8 cases match §4.7; upstream app_data tests 17/18 — test_app_data_update_multi_remove_validate_outgoing fails because its fixture removes component 16 without seeding it (fixture needs fixing).

Upstream test outline: (1) function-level ProposalQueue tests for a,b,c,d1,d2 with no GCE; (2) receiver-level test with frankenstein-crafted commit (re-sign, membership tag) expecting StageCommitError::AppDataUpdateValidationError; (3) fix the multi_remove fixture.

